{
  "duration": 397.2240000000123,
  "chapters": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 130.15200000000402
    },
    {
      "start": 130.15200000000402,
      "end": 262.96800000000815
    },
    {
      "start": 262.96800000000815,
      "end": 397.2240000000123
    }
  ],
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 1.440000057220459,
      "text": "Hey, welcome back.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 2.119999885559082,
      "end": 5.687179589882875,
      "text": "A fringe pattern carries two pieces of information: where the bright bands",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.687179589882875,
      "end": 5.880000114440918,
      "text": "sit,",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 5.880000114440918,
      "end": 8.359999656677246,
      "text": "and how strongly brightness changes between bands.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 9.100000381469727,
      "end": 10.260000228881836,
      "text": "Let's separate those ideas.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 11.220000267028809,
      "end": 14.779999732971191,
      "text": "Use two coherent, narrow sources with the same frequency and polarization.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 15.760000228881836,
      "end": 20.239999771118164,
      "text": "On our distant screen, define positive y so that the phase difference we use",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 20.239999771118164,
      "end": 21.260000228881836,
      "text": "increases with y.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 22.18000030517578,
      "end": 26.68000030517578,
      "text": "Write that phase as two pi times y divided by fringe width beta, plus a fixed",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 26.68000030517578,
      "end": 27.719999313354492,
      "text": "offset phi zero.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 28.84000015258789,
      "end": 32.730371404577184,
      "text": "Bright interference occurs when this total phase is an integer multiple of two",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 32.730371404577184,
      "end": 32.880001068115234,
      "text": "pi.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 33.47999954223633,
      "end": 36.79999923706055,
      "text": "A fixed offset moves the pattern but does not change the spacing.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 37.79999923706055,
      "end": 41.779998779296875,
      "text": "Take wavelength six hundred nanometres, screen distance one point five metres",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 42.31999969482422,
      "end": 45.279998779296875,
      "text": "and slit separation zero point nine millimetres.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 45.279998779296875,
      "end": 49.13999938964844,
      "text": "The small angle fringe width, wavelength times screen distance divided by slit",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 49.13999938964844,
      "end": 52,
      "text": "separation, is one millimetre.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 52,
      "end": 54.900001525878906,
      "text": "Now let the fixed phase offset be positive pi over two.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 55.540000915527344,
      "end": 56.939998626708984,
      "text": "Where is the zero phase bright order?",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 58.040000915527344,
      "end": 58.880001068115234,
      "text": "Pause and solve for y.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 59.459999084472656,
      "end": 63.63999938964844,
      "text": "It is negative beta over four, or negative zero point two five millimetres in",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 63.63999938964844,
      "end": 65,
      "text": "our declared coordinate convention.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 66.08000183105469,
      "end": 70.30000305175781,
      "text": "Reversing the sign convention changes the signed description, so never quote a",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 70.30000305175781,
      "end": 71.33999633789062,
      "text": "direction without defining it.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 72.0199966430664,
      "end": 75.47333583125362,
      "text": "Now make the two contributions have intensities nine and four units at the",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 75.47333583125362,
      "end": 75.80000305175781,
      "text": "screen.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 76.41999816894531,
      "end": 79.63999938964844,
      "text": "These are the separate intensities each would give there, not their source",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 79.63999938964844,
      "end": 80.04000091552734,
      "text": "powers.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 80.68000030517578,
      "end": 84.91999816894531,
      "text": "Superposition gives total intensity nine plus four plus twice the square root",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 84.91999816894531,
      "end": 86.76000213623047,
      "text": "of thirty six times cosine of the phase.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 87.23999786376953,
      "end": 89.77999877929688,
      "text": "At a bright order, the result is twenty five units.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 90.33999633789062,
      "end": 93.19999694824219,
      "text": "At an opposing phase, it is one unit, not zero.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 94,
      "end": 97.44000244140625,
      "text": "Perfect coherence does not guarantee perfect darkness when amplitudes differ.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 98.36000061035156,
      "end": 102,
      "text": "Fringe visibility compares the maximum minus minimum to the maximum plus",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 102,
      "end": 102.30000305175781,
      "text": "minimum.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 103.05999755859375,
      "end": 107.13948763333835,
      "text": "Here it is twenty four divided by twenty six, or twelve thirteenths, about",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 107.13948763333835,
      "end": 107.36000061035156,
      "text": "zero",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 107.36000061035156,
      "end": 109.37999725341797,
      "text": "point nine two three.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 109.37999725341797,
      "end": 113.0999984741211,
      "text": "Equal intensities would give unity visibility in this ideal fully overlapping",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 113.0999984741211,
      "end": 113.41999816894531,
      "text": "model.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 114.16000366210938,
      "end": 118.26000213623047,
      "text": "Poor coherence, mismatched polarization and detector averaging can also reduce",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 118.26000213623047,
      "end": 118.80000305175781,
      "text": "contrast.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 119.55999755859375,
      "end": 123.4000015258789,
      "text": "Our JEE routine is phase first for position, then the amplitude dependent",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 123.4000015258789,
      "end": 124.77999877929688,
      "text": "intensity formula for brightness.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 125.62000274658203,
      "end": 128.86000061035156,
      "text": "Do not mistake a shifted fringe or a nonzero minimum for proof that",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 128.86000061035156,
      "end": 129.8000030517578,
      "text": "interference has disappeared.",
      "chapter": 0
    },
    {
      "start": 130.15200000000402,
      "end": 133.87200002861425,
      "text": "Our earlier two slit model treated each slit as very narrow.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 134.71199994278356,
      "end": 137.81199984741613,
      "text": "Real slit width adds another layer: a diffraction envelope.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 138.75200038147375,
      "end": 142.2719998855631,
      "text": "Picture closely spaced interference ripples sitting inside a broader intensity",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 142.2719998855631,
      "end": 142.73199992371008,
      "text": "profile.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 143.9520001907389,
      "end": 148.19200091553137,
      "text": "Assume equal, uniformly illuminated rectangular slits, coherent equal phase",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 148.19200091553137,
      "end": 150.03199916077062,
      "text": "light, and far field conditions.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 150.9920001525919,
      "end": 154.43200068664953,
      "text": "Let each slit width be a and the centre to centre separation be d.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 155.3919997711222,
      "end": 159.2119994659464,
      "text": "Constructive interference orders obey d sine theta equals m wavelengths.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 160.35200076294348,
      "end": 165.03200106811926,
      "text": "Single slit envelope minima obey a sine theta equals p wavelengths, where p is",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 165.03200106811926,
      "end": 165.9920001525919,
      "text": "a nonzero integer.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 166.7719989318888,
      "end": 170.6720004577677,
      "text": "If both conditions hold at the same direction, the interference order has no",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 170.6720004577677,
      "end": 171.51200061035559,
      "text": "light to reinforce.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 172.01200061035559,
      "end": 172.57199816894934,
      "text": "It is missing.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 173.61199908447668,
      "end": 177.01200061035559,
      "text": "Dividing the two equations gives m equal to p times d over a.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 177.81199984741613,
      "end": 181.9920001525919,
      "text": "Try d equal to zero point six millimetres and a equal to zero point two",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 181.9920001525919,
      "end": 183.03200106811926,
      "text": "millimetres.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 183.03200106811926,
      "end": 184.3320003051798,
      "text": "Their ratio is three.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 185.11199908447668,
      "end": 189.4319987793009,
      "text": "Every third nonzero interference order coincides with an envelope minimum in",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 189.4319987793009,
      "end": 190.19200091553137,
      "text": "this ideal model.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 190.9319987793009,
      "end": 194.95636060979217,
      "text": "In particular, orders positive three and negative three are absent at the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 194.95636060979217,
      "end": 195.2320018310587,
      "text": "first",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 195.2320018310587,
      "end": 195.97199969482824,
      "text": "envelope boundaries.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 197.45200305176184,
      "end": 201.3519969482462,
      "text": "Now use wavelength six hundred nanometres and screen distance one point five",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 201.3519969482462,
      "end": 202.031997253422,
      "text": "metres.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 202.97199969482824,
      "end": 205.69200091553137,
      "text": "Interference spacing is one point five millimetres.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 205.69200091553137,
      "end": 209.25815089612533,
      "text": "The first diffraction minima lie four point five millimetres from the centre",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 209.25815089612533,
      "end": 209.3519969482462,
      "text": "on",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 209.3519969482462,
      "end": 213.57199816894934,
      "text": "either side, so the full central envelope width is nine millimetres.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 213.57199816894934,
      "end": 216.71199755859777,
      "text": "How many principal interference orders fit strictly inside it?",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 217.65200000000402,
      "end": 218.11199908447668,
      "text": "Take a moment.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 218.89199786377355,
      "end": 222.77200274658605,
      "text": "Their labels are negative two, negative one, zero, positive one and positive",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 222.77200274658605,
      "end": 223.3320003051798,
      "text": "two.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 223.89199786377355,
      "end": 225.07199816894934,
      "text": "Five, not seven.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 225.71199755859777,
      "end": 227.95200305176184,
      "text": "The boundary orders are dark and must not be counted.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 228.67199664307043,
      "end": 230.61199908447668,
      "text": "The envelope also makes the outer peaks weaker.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 231.29199938965246,
      "end": 235.65200000000402,
      "text": "For a mathematical intensity sketch, multiply cosine squared of pi d y over",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 235.65200000000402,
      "end": 240.9319987793009,
      "text": "wavelength D by the squared sine over argument envelope, using argument pi a y",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 240.9319987793009,
      "end": 242.01200061035559,
      "text": "over wavelength D.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 242.59200244141027,
      "end": 246.55200152588293,
      "text": "At zero argument, that envelope equals one by its limit; don't let your",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 246.55200152588293,
      "end": 248.09200244141027,
      "text": "calculator divide zero by zero.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 248.71199755859777,
      "end": 252.27200274658605,
      "text": "The envelope can shift actual local peak positions slightly away from the",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 252.27200274658605,
      "end": 253.3519969482462,
      "text": "narrow slit order positions.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 254.031997253422,
      "end": 257.3519969482462,
      "text": "Our five order count is the standard interference order description.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 258.3319926757853,
      "end": 261.8920054931681,
      "text": "Distinguish fringe spacing, full central envelope width, and actual peak",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 261.8920054931681,
      "end": 262.96800000000815,
      "text": "brightness: they are different quantities in one pattern.",
      "chapter": 1
    },
    {
      "start": 262.96800000000815,
      "end": 265.30799991417746,
      "text": "Let's finish with a lovely optical puzzle.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 266.2479999713979,
      "end": 269.0279999427877,
      "text": "Two ideal crossed polarizers block the transmitted beam.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 269.82800013352255,
      "end": 273.0479999237142,
      "text": "Put another polarizer between them, and some light can come through.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 273.68800026703695,
      "end": 275.6480003051839,
      "text": "Does that mean the extra sheet creates energy?",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 276.22800022889,
      "end": 277.1679998092733,
      "text": "Absolutely not.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 277.80800015259604,
      "end": 281.58800083924154,
      "text": "Each sheet still reduces or preserves the intensity arriving at that sheet.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 282.12799984742026,
      "end": 286.08800083924154,
      "text": "It changes the selected polarization direction, which changes what the later",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 286.08800083924154,
      "end": 286.84799916077475,
      "text": "sheet can transmit.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 287.96800000000815,
      "end": 290.72800022889,
      "text": "Start with unpolarized light of intensity one hundred units.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 291.1480003051839,
      "end": 295.28799969483237,
      "text": "The first axis is zero degrees and the final axis is ninety degrees.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 296.22799832154135,
      "end": 298.68800122071127,
      "text": "The first ideal sheet passes fifty units.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 299.5879989318929,
      "end": 301.3280006103597,
      "text": "Insert one middle axis at angle theta.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 302.02800137329916,
      "end": 306.46800000000815,
      "text": "That sheet passes fifty times cosine squared theta, and the last passes that",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 306.46800000000815,
      "end": 308.02800137329916,
      "text": "result times sine squared theta.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 308.9880004577718,
      "end": 312.78799969483237,
      "text": "Using the double angle relation, final intensity is one hundred divided by",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 312.78799969483237,
      "end": 314.9880004577718,
      "text": "eight, times sine squared of twice theta.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 315.6680007629476,
      "end": 317.3280006103597,
      "text": "What angle gives the greatest output?",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 318.18800122071127,
      "end": 318.88799816895346,
      "text": "Pause before choosing.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 318.88799816895346,
      "end": 323.78799969483237,
      "text": "Forty five degrees makes that squared sine one, so the maximum is twelve point",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 323.78799969483237,
      "end": 324.6079993896566,
      "text": "five units.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 325.3280006103597,
      "end": 329.7126136474691,
      "text": "The final beam is polarized along the final sheet's ninety degree axis, not",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 329.7126136474691,
      "end": 329.88799816895346,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 329.88799816895346,
      "end": 330.8479972534261,
      "text": "middle sheet's axis.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 331.78799969483237,
      "end": 336.88799816895346,
      "text": "Now use two middle sheets instead, giving successive axes zero, thirty, sixty",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 336.88799816895346,
      "end": 337.7079978637777,
      "text": "and ninety degrees.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 338.4080024414144,
      "end": 341.0880027465902,
      "text": "Each step after the first differs by thirty degrees.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 341.747998779305,
      "end": 343.9080024414144,
      "text": "Cosine squared thirty degrees is three quarters.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 344.7280021362386,
      "end": 349.2180019073568,
      "text": "Track the sequence: fifty units, thirty seven point five, twenty eight point",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 349.2180019073568,
      "end": 353.76800305176596,
      "text": "one two five, and finally twenty one point zero nine three seven five units.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 354.54800183106283,
      "end": 358.54800183106283,
      "text": "More than twelve point five, but every individual step still lost light.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 359.16799694825033,
      "end": 363.0279975586019,
      "text": "If you swap or reorder the sheets, their successive angle differences change",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 363.3280006103597,
      "end": 364.4279990844808,
      "text": "and the result can change.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 365.1480003051839,
      "end": 368.94800335694174,
      "text": "If the original beam is already polarized, do not automatically halve its",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 368.94800335694174,
      "end": 373.04800183106283,
      "text": "intensity at the first sheet.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 373.04800183106283,
      "end": 374.38799816895346,
      "text": "Use the angle between its actual polarization and that first axis.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 375.0880027465902,
      "end": 379.26800305176596,
      "text": "These are ideal monochromatic teaching models; real sheets have losses and",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 379.26800305176596,
      "end": 382.5677487068258,
      "text": "leakage, so adding many sheets is not a promise of unlimited useful",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 382.5677487068258,
      "end": 383.2079978637777,
      "text": "transmission.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 383.96800000000815,
      "end": 388.6480003051839,
      "text": "For JEE problems, draw the axes in order, update polarization after each",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 388.6480003051839,
      "end": 391.4080024414144,
      "text": "filter, and multiply the correct intensity factors.",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 392.30799633789877,
      "end": 396.03877026368,
      "text": "Tracking the intermediate state is more reliable than applying one angle to",
      "chapter": 2
    },
    {
      "start": 396.03877026368,
      "end": 396.18800122071127,
      "text": "the",
      "chapter": 2
    },
